# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [2.0.0] - ???

This new release brings a major update to Honocord's architecture, introducing a new handler system for both interactions and webhooks. This allows for more modular, flexible, and type-safe development.

This brings along some breaking changes, so please review the migration guide in the docs.

### Added

- `WebhookEventHandler` class for handling Discord webhook events with type safety (It's a Hono app under the hood, so you can use it standalone or with the bot) - [Read the docs](https://honocord.thelukez.com/guides/webhook-events)

### Changed

- Expanded `Honocord` class to support loading both interaction handlers and webhook handlers
- Changed the returned hono app from `Honocord.getApp()` to now include both interaction and webhook routes: **The routing changed!**
  - Interactions are now routed to `/interactions` and `/` (for legacy support)
  - Webhooks are routed to `/webhook`

- Customizable paths for both interactions and webhooks via `getApp({ interactionsPath, webhookPath })` (defaults to `/interactions` and `/webhook`)
- Restructured internal handler management and types

## [1.4.0] - 2026-02-04

### Added

- Separate interaction classes for different component types (e.g., ButtonInteraction, StringSelectMenuInteraction, etc.) for better type safety and clarity

### Changed

- Order of generic parameters in ComponentHandler to have Context first, improving consistency with other handlers
- Updated dependencies to latest versions

## [1.3.2] - 2026-01-26

### Fixed

- Middleware chain not executing handlers properly - middleware now correctly calls `next()` to continue the chain

## [1.3.1] - 2026-01-26

### Fixed

- Middleware not accepting custom context types

## [1.3.0] - 2026-01-26

### Added

- Middleware functionality
- Improved typings for better developer experience
